# Keeps the Docker build context to the sources the image actually needs.
#
# Without this the context is ~472 MB, because app.Dockerfile does `COPY . .` and this directory
# carries 579 MB of node_modules and 27 MB of target/. Those are the two that matter:
#
#   node_modules — reinstalled by `npm ci` inside the image, from the lockfile. Copying the host's
#                  copy in is wasted transfer at best; at worst it carries platform-specific native
#                  builds from a different OS into the build stage.
#   target/      — the previous build's output. The image runs `npm run webapp:prod`, which starts
#                  by clearing it, so shipping it in is pure cost.
#
# Modelled on hc-admin-dashboard's .dockerignore, which this repository never had.
**/.classpath
**/.dockerignore
**/.env
**/.git
**/.gitignore
**/.project
**/.settings
**/.toolstarget
**/.vs
**/.vscode
**/*.*proj.user
**/*.dbmdl
**/*.jfm
**/bin
**/charts
**/docker-compose*
**/compose*
**/Dockerfile*
**/node_modules
**/npm-debug.log
**/obj
**/secrets.dev.yaml
**/values.dev.yaml
LICENSE
README.md

# Build output. `webapp:prod` clears and regenerates it inside the image.
target
